# Milestone progress

When the task is an open milestone on `https://github.com/taveraos/taveraos`, update that milestone in GitHub in the same turn as the work. Match it by title (`Milestone 16: The next application`). The number in the title is not the GitHub milestone number.

Use `gh --repo taveraos/taveraos`. Leave `https://github.com/reactos/reactos` alone. Do not open, close, or retitle a milestone. If the task fits more than one open milestone, ask Ryan which one. Work that is not a milestone stays off the milestone list.

## Progress

Read the milestone description before changing it.

When one task bullet is finished, change that line from `-` to `- [x]`. While a task is unfinished, leave its bullet and replace the `## Progress` section at the end with the current state: the date, the task, what is done, and the issue number. Leave the goal, the other tasks, and the success criteria as they are.

Write the description back with `gh api --method PATCH`. Read it back. Stop if any line outside that bullet and the `## Progress` section changed.

## Issues

Do not open a GitHub issue unless Ryan asks for one. A fault found while
carrying the milestone out is recorded in Progress and fixed in the same
loop; it is not filed automatically.

When Ryan asks to open an issue, or an issue already exists for the fault:

- Search the milestone's open issues first. Comment on the existing issue when it is the same fault.
- A new issue title is `[MODULE] Imperative summary`. The body is the symptom, the check that showed it, and the task it blocks. Add the `bug` label for a defect. Set `--milestone` to the milestone title.
- Close the issue when Ryan asks, or when the same check no longer shows the fault and the close is part of finishing that slice. The close comment names that check.
- Leave the issue open when the fix is not verified yet. One issue is one fault. Do not file an issue that restates the milestone.

```text
Wrong: gh issue create during a silent-fail fix loop without Ryan asking
Right: fix the fault; update Progress; open an issue only when Ryan says to
Right: gh issue close 42 --repo taveraos/taveraos --comment "The import resolves. The installer reaches the desktop."
```
